# Build-time configuration. Vite reads this file automatically, so a local
# build, a CI build and a release build all get the same values with no setup.
#
# **Nothing secret goes in here, and this file is committed on purpose.**
# The repository is public and every value below is compiled into the shipped
# bundle, so anything put here is published twice over. A password, a token
# that can read something, or a signing key would belong in the repository's
# Actions secrets instead — and none of those exist in this project.

# Which Aptabase app the usage reporting belongs to. See Settings → Privacy in
# the app, and docs/plan.md → Phase 29 for what is reported and what is not.
#
# **An Aptabase app key is not a secret and is designed to be shipped.** It is
# write-only: it says where events go, and it cannot read a single thing back
# out. Every client that reports anything carries one, which is why theirs is
# documented as public rather than protected. Keeping it out of the repository
# would achieve nothing — it would still be sitting in the installer.
#
# What it does allow is somebody who finds it sending junk events, which would
# show up as noise on the dashboard. That is the accepted cost of any
# client-side analytics and there is no version of this without it. If the
# numbers are ever obviously poisoned, roll the key in the Aptabase dashboard
# and change it here.
VITE_APTABASE_KEY=A-US-2279710351
